Notes on Recode File

1.   Husbands are included in this file whether or not they are DEFACTO
     residents of the household.
2.   Four men who were eligible respondents were not entered into the raw
     data.
3.   MV034 has been corrected from the raw data file where incorrect line
     numbers of wives appear.
4.   MV312 has been corrected from the raw data for the cases that were
     missing method currently being used and following skips for non-users.
     These cases have been coded as non-users.
5.   For one case, MV602 has been corrected to missing from not applicable.
6.   For eight cases, MV610, MV611, MV612 and MV621 were corrected to missing
     from not applicable.
7.   There are 18 cases for which MV628 and MV629 do not sum to MV613.  This
     is because the code of 30 for MV613 represents 30+ children.
8.   MV009 and MV507 (imputed month of birth and marriage) are skewed.
9.   There are 55 cases in which the respondentþs wife has an incomplete
     questionnaire.

Inconsistencies in the Data File

1.   There is one case in which MV801 equals 0 minutes; there is one case  in
     which MV801 equals less than 0 minutes; there are two cases in which
     MV801 is greater than 180 minutes.
2.   These is one case in which ever use of female sterilization is reported
     but is not currently being used.
3.   There is one case in which there is an inconsistency between the wifeþs
     report of her husbandþs line number and his report of his wifeþs line
     number.
4.   There are 18 men who are reported as eligible for interview in the
     household roster who are not present in the husbandþs data file.

